context_info = ()
for d in context:
    result = llm_query("You will be given a single document. Analyze it to see if it matches either of two target articles, and extract key facts. Use only what is in the document plus widely known facts like a major media company's founding year. Be precise and include short quotes from the document where relevant.\n\nTARGET A (2019 article):\n- Description: An article published in November 2019 by a media company founded in the 1960s. The article discusses different scoring methods for various types of the same sport. The article references only one professional athlete by name throughout the entire article.\n- If the document matches this, extract: publisher/media company; its founding year; publication date; the sport; the different scoring methods/types discussed; the single professional athlete's full name; a brief quote that shows the athlete's name appears; and confirm that it is the only professional athlete named.\n\nTARGET B (2020 article):\n- Description: An article published in January 2020 by a media company that originated in the 1950s, about the athlete identified in TARGET A, that includes excerpts from an interview with the athlete.\n- If the document matches this, extract: publisher/media company; its founding year; publication date; athlete's full name; clear indication that it contains interview excerpts; and the athlete's hometown as stated in the article, with an exact quote showing the hometown wording.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nDocument Summary:\n- Detected title/headline (if present):\n- Detected publisher/media company (if present or inferable):\n- Publisher founding year (if known):\n- Detected publication date (if present):\n- Sport(s) discussed (if any):\n\nTarget A (Nov 2019 scoring article) Assessment:\n- Matches Target A: Yes/No\n- Athlete named (if matches):\n- Sport and scoring types referenced (if matches):\n- Evidence quotes (include the athlete name line and scoring discussion lines):\n- Notes:\n\nTarget B (Jan 2020 interview article) Assessment:\n- Matches Target B: Yes/No\n- Athlete (if matches):\n- Media company and founding year (if matches):\n- Publication date (if matches):\n- Interview excerpt evidence (short quote):\n- Hometown as stated (exact wording in quotes):\n- Evidence quotes for hometown:\n\nBegin Document:\n" + d + "\nEnd Document.")
    context_info = context_info + (result,)

synthesis = llm_query("You will be given multiple per-document analyses. Your task is to determine the athlete and their hometown based on the following logic:\n\n1) Identify which document(s) match TARGET A: an article published in November 2019 by a media company founded in the 1960s, discussing different scoring methods for various types of the same sport, and that names exactly one professional athlete. Extract that athlete's full name.\n2) Using that athlete, identify which document(s) match TARGET B: an article published in January 2020 by a media company that originated in the 1950s, containing interview excerpts with that athlete. From that specific 2020 article, extract the athlete's hometown exactly as stated in the article text.\n3) Output ONLY the hometown string exactly as it appears in the 2020 article. Do not include any additional words, labels, punctuation, or explanation. If you cannot determine the hometown from the provided analyses, output exactly: Unknown\n\nHere are the analyses:\n" + "\n\n-----\n\n".join(context_info))

return_result(synthesis.strip())